  14 |  0.2997 |         0.1022 |     0.0173 |       0.3409 |      0.3986
  16 |  0.2157 |         0.0709 |     0.0097 |       0.3286 |      0.3735
  20 |  0.1276 |         0.0397 |     0.0038 |       0.3111 |      0.3409

  MEASURED, not asserted: at n = 10 the LINEAR share is 0.379 and the
  total Lemma-B exposure 0.488 -- about a third linear and about half in
  total, falling to 0.311 and 0.341 by n = 20.  (An earlier draft of
  this line said 'roughly three quarters', which the table does not
  support; the numbers above are the numbers.)  So the constant matters
  to about half the column, not to almost all of it -- which is already
  a hint at PART 4's answer.

