PART 4.  WHAT A SHARPER LEMMA B WOULD BUY.
   c    | honest threshold
   1.00 | 9
   1.25 | 9
   1.50 | 9
   1.63 | 10
   2.00 | 10
   2.34 | 10
   2.53 | 10
   3.00 | 11
   4.00 | 11

  THE ANSWER TO THE DECIDING QUESTION.  The honest threshold is FLAT at
  n >= 10 across the entire admissible range 1.63 <= c <= 2.53.  Since
  the real geometry forces c >= 1.63, and my own crude substitute
  (c = 2.76 at n = 10) already lands on 10, sharpening Lemma B buys
  NOTHING for the honest column.  Only c <= 1.5 would give 9, and the
  constructed violation rules that out.
  BUT IT DOES HELP THE CONDITIONAL COLUMN: 9 with my substitute, 8 with
  pincer's cap.  The conditional core4 uses the parked eps and so is
  Lemma-B-free, but y3q and y3l still ride on sqrt(M_z), and at n = 8
  my substitute's c = 3.41 against the cap's 2.53 is the whole
  difference.  So the cap is worth one step, on the conditional route
  only.

